# =============================================================================
# IP PROTECTION — DO NOT REMOVE OR LOOSEN THESE RULES WITHOUT REVIEW
# =============================================================================
# This repository must never contain disc data, extracted assets, or any
# material owned by Sony Interactive Entertainment / Team Ico.
# The rules below ignore every common PS2 dump and extracted-asset format.
# If you need to add a real source file whose name happens to collide, prefer
# renaming the file rather than weakening the patterns.
# =============================================================================

# --- Disc images and PS2 executables ---
*.bin
*.iso
*.cue
*.chd
*.mdf
*.mds
*.nrg
*.elf
*.irx
SLUS-*
SLES-*
SLPS-*
SLPM-*
SCUS-*
SCES-*
SCPS-*
baserom/
baseelf*

# --- Build outputs that may embed disc-derived data ---
build/
*.o
*.a
*.lib
*.obj
*.map
*.ld.tmp

# --- Extracted assets (populated at build time from the user's disc) ---
assets/**
!assets/.gitkeep
!assets/README.md

# --- Audio / texture / model dumps ---
*.aifc
*.aiff
*.wav
*.adp
*.vag
*.vab
*.mid
*.seq
*.tm2
*.png.bin
*.rgba16
*.rgba32

# --- Symbol files derived from the original ELF ---
# (Symbol *names* invented by us are fine; raw vendor symbol tables are not.)
*.sym.bak

# --- Toolchain / venv / editor noise ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Local config overrides ---
.env
.env.local
config/local.*
expected/

# --- m2c context output (regenerated on demand) ---
ctx.c

# --- Local toolchain blobs (Ghidra, ee-gcc, ps2toolchain source build) ---
tools/toolchain/
tools/ghidra/
tools/cc/

# --- Agent guidance / local-only ---
# CLAUDE.md is auto-loaded by Claude Code and is the agent's local preamble;
# kept out of the public repo to match the snap project's convention.
# docs/MATCH.md is the public, user-facing matching prompt.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
docs/RUN_LOG.md
# Ninja build files: the manifest is written by tools/gen_ninja.py from
# config/link_order.pal.txt on every `tools/build.sh setup`. The .ninja_log
# and .ninja_deps are runtime state.
build.ninja
build.plain.ninja
.ninja_log
.ninja_deps

# --- Cross-target knowledge docs — shared across branches, local-only ---
# These are the accumulated, target-INDEPENDENT matching wisdom (cookbook,
# notes, matching guides, legal/build references). They apply equally to the
# PAL retail target (this branch, `main`), the USA retail target (`ntsc`) and
# the Aug-6-2001 prototype (`aug6`). To avoid divergence/merge pain and keep a
# single physical copy that `git checkout` never clobbers, they are gitignored +
# untracked (same convention as CLAUDE.md / .claude/). Edit them freely on any
# branch; the one working-tree copy is shared. History up to the untrack commit
# lives in the repo; go-forward changes are local-only.
docs/COOKBOOK.md
docs/NOTES.md
docs/ARCHIVE_retired_notes.md
docs/MATCH.md
docs/MATCH-FAST.md
docs/MATCH_DATA.md
docs/MATCH_VU.md
docs/PROMOTE.md
docs/struct_shapes.md
docs/header_candidates.md
docs/RODATA_PHASE3D.md
docs/RODATA_ROADMAP.md
docs/multi_tu_slices.md
docs/LEGAL.md
docs/BUILDING.md
docs/MATCHING_NOTES.md

# Retail->aug6 port-audit artifacts (normalized-asm twin map, 2026-06-08).
# Local-only.
docs/retail_port
# aug6 data-phase investigation report (local working note).
docs/DATA_INVESTIGATION.md

# Pre-merge home of everything above: the old decomp/ directory folded into
# docs/. Anything still sitting there is a local leftover, never a tracked path.
/decomp/

# Assembled GitHub Pages site (regenerable: .github/scripts/build_pages_site.sh).
_site/

# supervisor round-by-round ledger (kept outside the repo)
docs/convergence_chain_ledger.md

# PAL listing-derived source-structure census (docs/pal_source_tree.*): local-only,
# derived from the disc's listing in baserom/pal/; bulk metadata stays out of git.
docs/pal_source_tree.md
docs/pal_source_tree.json

# Local caches (regenerable; never committed)
.cache/
.port_cache/
.transplant_cache/
